  "term": "autonomy",
  "definition": "Autonomy means independence or self-determination, especially freedom from outside control or restraint. In discussions of the will, it can mean either complete freedom or a relative freedom from motives imposed by others, and in Kantian usage it refers to the rational will as giving law to itself.",
